WEBVTT

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:32.220
I don't like this.

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:34.680
It's almost over.

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:37.050
<i>ENTER THE RED DOORS</i>

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:36.730
We can only move forward.

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:41.140
This is Kanzaki.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:57.660
<i>Up above the forest of slumber</i>

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:53.110
It's an unbelievable sight.

00:00:53.110 --> 00:00:56.820
White lilies are blooming,
and the sky has turned ominous.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:04.290
<i>Two moons look down from the sky</i>

00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:00.530
It's like the dream world...

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:02.010
White lilies...?

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:06.400
Dreams are spilling over
into the real world.

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:11.800
<i>Where did you come from,</i>
<i>and where are you going?</i>

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:08.660
Because Eve's awake?

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:10.250
How's Haruto?

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:11.510
Well...

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:20.180
<i>Where are we going?</i>

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:15.760
This is Eve's awakening!

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:19.510
People, sleep in this
pure world for Eve's sake!

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:24.730
Fall into an eternal sleep cushioned
by white lilies and embraced by Eve's scent!

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:25.850
<i>ENTER THE RED DOORS</i>

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:26.690
Yes, release your souls,

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:30.060
and become truly free!

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:34.230
"Eve's Sigh"

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:37.710
Put this on.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:39.320
Why?

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:42.740
Yuko, repeat what you just said.

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:45.080
Let Haruto hear it, too.

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:50.330
Haruto has been in a coma
for a long, long time.

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:55.630
According to the records, he was
in an accident and fell into a coma,

00:01:55.630 --> 00:01:57.280
as if hibernating...

00:01:58.260 --> 00:01:59.890
It's not clear what caused it.

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:03.240
Do you remember the accident?

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:04.550
No.

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:07.810
Brother, you're the only one
different from everyone else.

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:09.690
Time doesn't move for you.

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:11.980
Then, it's the same as if I were dead.

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:21.550
Eve! More! Bloom in your glory!

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:28.580
Oh, Eve! Release us impure
beings with your awakening!

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:32.740
Oh, Eve! Oh, Eve! Release me!

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:40.860
Since time was stopped for you,

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:43.850
you were just in an endless 
cycle in the dream world.

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:46.060
It was the same for Eve.

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:47.860
She just kept repeating the regret she had

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:49.890
for eating the fruit of 
the Tree of Knowledge.

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:52.310
I don't care why it's me anymore.

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:56.230
More importantly, if we don't do something
about Eve, everyone's gonna die, right?

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:58.860
That's why our only option is to kill Eve.

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:00.360
Then <i>you</i> do it.

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:03.530
You're the one who knows Eve best, right?

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:05.370
I <i>am</i> Eve.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:15.310
Beyond this door lies Eve.

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:17.050
Wait a sec.

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:18.010
You're Eve?

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:19.870
I'm the other Eve.

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:23.310
The Eve of Eden, before she
ate the fruit of the Tree of Knowledge.

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:27.890
The Eve that received God's
blessings and laughed with Adam.

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:31.940
If we finish Eve off, will I wake up?

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:37.040
I'm not alive, but I'm not dead, either.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:38.780
Then, what am I?

00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:42.340
If you kill Eve for me,
then you'll know the answer.

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:43.980
What'll happen to you?

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:47.530
I am Eve. I will die with her.

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:56.550
Huh?

00:04:00.710 --> 00:04:02.400
Isn't this your room?

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:03.510
Yeah...

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:05.980
Why are we in Brother's room?

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:18.640
Um, who are you?

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:20.320
That's Eve.

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:20.940
Eve?

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:22.290
This is?

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:26.450
What a strange room.

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:28.740
It lacks beauty.

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:30.580
Such a dull room.

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:32.790
She's different from what I imagined.

00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:33.710
Yeah...

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:35.260
This is your room?

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:36.480
Yeah.

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:41.070
You know, Lily, I can see through
everything you're thinking.

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:46.140
However, nothing you can do
will cause me to falter.

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:48.380
I have a long-standing grudge.

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:52.770
I will completely destroy
this world that God created.

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:54.440
I won't let you.

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:55.690
Die.

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:00.020
Don't fight.

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:02.440
You're both Eve, right?

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:03.390
Indeed.

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:05.860
As such, one is enough.

00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:20.920
Yurina?

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:22.210
I ended up coming.

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:23.590
Everyone...

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:25.470
The witches... Why?

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:30.300
We were saved by Haruto.

00:05:30.890 --> 00:05:33.560
So <i>we</i> will save <i>him</i> this time.

00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:36.730
He saved you, you say?

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:38.560
How ridiculous!

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:41.800
Having a man save you!
You should be ashamed!

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:48.770
Listen, did you know that according
to God's order, women are to obey men?

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:50.450
This is absurd!

00:05:50.440 --> 00:05:52.120
Oh, is that so?

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:55.830
That's so old-fashioned.
Women obeying men and such.

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:57.460
Who decided that?

00:05:58.000 --> 00:05:58.760
God did.

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:01.750
Doesn't that kind of make you mad?

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:02.500
Evie.

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:03.800
"Evie"?!

00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:08.680
I got kind of a revelation just now,
but you know, for me and Yureena,

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:14.260
frankly, our popularity depends on how much
we butter those guys up, you know?

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:16.270
Like when I get the lyrics
to a new song, sometimes I think,

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:19.690
"Whoa, this is what makes
guys happy? Gross."

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:20.350
Stuff like that.

00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:22.940
Ah, Misaki, you're being too honest...

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:25.190
I do not quite understand.

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:26.990
Listen, Evie-pie.

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:28.490
"Evie-pie"?

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:30.820
Oh, that's cute!

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:31.950
Didn't expect that from you, Yuko.

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:33.560
You say stuff like that?

00:06:33.990 --> 00:06:36.750
Well, I do like cute things.

00:06:37.450 --> 00:06:42.000
Evie-pie, we are here for our own sakes.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.750
Then, maybe I'll call her Evette.

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:46.510
"Evette"?

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:51.340
Anyway, women obeying men
is way out of date.

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:53.800
These days, women decide everything.

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:56.310
Men are like their servants,
you know. Servants.

00:06:56.770 --> 00:06:57.700
Bingo.

00:06:58.140 --> 00:06:58.930
Oh?

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:03.270
Then there is a gap between
God's will and the human world?

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:06.480
Aren't you all getting a little too friendly?

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:11.200
She's saying that we
should hear her out first.

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:13.280
You mean, have a discussion?

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:15.530
Why don't we try leaving it to the witches?

00:07:15.530 --> 00:07:17.290
Even you're saying that?

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:20.870
Haruto and the professor
can watch from over there.

00:07:20.870 --> 00:07:23.210
Oh, Big Brother, prepare some tea!

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:24.080
Tea?!

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:24.960
And some snacks.

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:25.880
Snacks?!

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:27.710
Do you have any?

00:07:27.710 --> 00:07:30.090
Well, I do have some...

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:34.090
Why do you need tea and snacks?

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:36.060
We're gonna have some girls' talk, right?

00:07:36.060 --> 00:07:37.600
We definitely need some.

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:39.430
Evie-pie, what would you like?

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:41.390
What is "tea"?

00:07:41.390 --> 00:07:45.440
Oh, my, I don't know how old you are,
but you can have alcohol, if you want.

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:49.400
Oh, but if she doesn't know what teatime is,
we should let her experience it.

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:52.780
There's coffee and green tea,
black tea and herb tea...

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:54.780
Let's have them prepare
a lot of different kinds.

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:57.030
You heard her, Big Brother!
Thanks a bunch!

00:07:57.030 --> 00:07:59.040
What do you mean, "Thanks a bunch"?!

00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:05.420
Big Brother, don't forget
the milk and sugar.

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:07.800
I will have some herb tea.

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:08.770
What about you, Suono?

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:12.220
Do you have cinnamon?

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:14.410
You girls are sure working this cat hard...

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:16.470
Evette, what about you?

00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:19.640
What's the matter?

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:22.310
This is wonderful.

00:08:22.690 --> 00:08:26.690
Did you see that, God?
Men are attending the women!

00:08:26.690 --> 00:08:29.710
This is lovely. I win!

00:08:38.030 --> 00:08:40.490
It's like you two are
working at a butler cafe.

00:08:40.490 --> 00:08:41.580
I didn't think you'd know about those.

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:45.540
This is delicious, this thing you call "tea."

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:47.250
But this isn't that good.

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:49.290
Is that so?

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:52.260
Haruto, this tea's kind of weak.

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:53.510
You're pretty demanding.

00:08:53.670 --> 00:08:55.630
Shall we try changing
the amount of tealeaves?

00:08:56.260 --> 00:08:58.510
Seems like something you'd like.

00:08:58.510 --> 00:09:00.470
The scientist's blood in me clamors.

00:09:00.470 --> 00:09:04.690
I yearn to know what mixture will bring
the most happiness to their tongues...

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:05.520
I see.

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:08.690
This is truly exhilarating.

00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:13.610
Even God would be surprised
at this relationship.

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:18.530
But why were you talking about silly
things like women obeying men?

00:09:18.530 --> 00:09:22.080
Saying stuff like that these days'll
cause a flame war online.

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:25.510
Why must women obey men?

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:30.090
We must go back in time to when
I was tempted by the snake.

00:09:30.090 --> 00:09:33.920
I see. Since you were
the one tempted, Evie-pie,

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:37.300
God decided that you were a fool, right?

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:43.090
Yes. Consequently, humans were
burdened with pain and suffering.

00:09:44.560 --> 00:09:46.210
It must be ended.

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:51.110
Destroying it with my own hands
is my way of taking responsibility.

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:53.270
Oh, I get that.

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:54.870
Natsuki!

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:59.200
It was the same for me
when I was being bullied.

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:01.620
It was my own fault that
it ended up like that...

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:02.970
I was wrong...

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:05.620
I was gradually made to feel that way.

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:07.870
Oh, yes! That's exactly it.

00:10:07.870 --> 00:10:12.540
But you know, Evonne. If you start
thinking like that, you'll lose.

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:13.430
"Evonne"?

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:16.800
But it's not your fault, Leapy Eve.

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:18.740
What's this "leapy" thing?

00:10:19.220 --> 00:10:22.300
The snake is the one at fault.
You were tricked.

00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:25.570
Therefore, since I was tricked, I was a fool.

00:10:26.890 --> 00:10:30.100
That's why we're saying that
you can't think like that!

00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:30.810
But--

00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:32.340
No buts about it.

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:36.240
You just made one mistake.
You're worrying too much about it.

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:37.610
Do you understand, Evelyn?

00:10:38.240 --> 00:10:39.120
"Evelyn"...

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:45.410
You have some nerve, all of you,
changing my name one after the other.

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:49.000
But you know, it was because of what I did

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:51.870
that women came to bear pain and suffering.

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:53.570
That's true.

00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:56.390
We really do suffer.

00:10:57.050 --> 00:10:58.590
From hopeless illnesses...

00:10:59.050 --> 00:11:00.970
...and conflicts that never end.

00:11:00.970 --> 00:11:02.010
Right?

00:11:02.010 --> 00:11:04.960
But... there are a lot of fun things, too.

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:08.020
Having all of that is what makes us human.

00:11:08.310 --> 00:11:10.980
We are not perfect like God is,

00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:14.040
but those mistakes are part
of who we are as humans.

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:16.410
I know you...

00:11:18.030 --> 00:11:20.510
Didn't you fight against the fear of death?

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:25.330
I did, but I was able
to gain some courage,

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:28.950
so I was able to live my
fullest in the time I had left.

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:33.530
Eve, I'd like you to get courage from us.

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:37.440
You should just change your perspective.

00:11:38.010 --> 00:11:39.190
What do you mean?

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:43.430
Anger and irritation make
your own world smaller.

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:45.670
Just by changing your point of view a bit,

00:11:45.670 --> 00:11:47.650
you can make your world open up, you know,

00:11:47.650 --> 00:11:48.970
Evie-Evie.

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:54.690
You all were able to escape
the dream world like that, huh?

00:11:55.400 --> 00:11:58.980
However, my anger is not something
that can be extinguished so easily.

00:12:00.110 --> 00:12:01.980
It's not something that can be forgiven.

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:04.740
I do feel like I understand...

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:09.620
Your anger is on a
different scale from ours.

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:11.870
That's true.

00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:15.710
Well, it's not something that
can go away so easily, huh?

00:12:16.590 --> 00:12:18.660
At times like that, you want
to launch a counterattack, right?

00:12:19.960 --> 00:12:21.290
You should do it.

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:23.390
You are...

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:26.820
Resentment isn't something
that will just disappear.

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:28.720
It'll keep following you around.

00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:31.430
I'm on your side.

00:12:31.430 --> 00:12:33.520
You should just destroy everything.

00:12:33.520 --> 00:12:35.900
Hey, that's too scary!

00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:41.580
Why? This person's soul will not
be cleansed until the world is destroyed.

00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:45.190
That's right.

00:12:45.820 --> 00:12:48.660
I must accomplish my objective, after all.

00:12:48.870 --> 00:12:51.160
Hey, isn't this bad?

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:54.140
It seems like everyone's
starting to agree with Eve.

00:12:58.290 --> 00:13:00.310
Everyone, do you understand now?

00:13:00.750 --> 00:13:02.550
That is what the dream world is.

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:04.780
A world where anyone can become God.

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:09.320
But that's lonely, Evvy.

00:13:10.430 --> 00:13:11.520
Jane.

00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:13.320
Those around you may

00:13:13.320 --> 00:13:16.550
not think you messed up
as much as you think you did, you know?

00:13:17.520 --> 00:13:18.400
What?

00:13:18.770 --> 00:13:22.820
I am thankful that you ate the
fruit of the Tree of Knowledge.

00:13:23.530 --> 00:13:27.280
Thanks to you, humans are able
to have many different emotions.

00:13:27.280 --> 00:13:29.450
Because we experience sadness, we can smile.

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:32.890
Because we can smile,
tears have worth, too.

00:13:35.710 --> 00:13:39.000
Humans cannot return to
the Garden of Eden anymore.

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:41.420
No, they do not <i>want</i> to return.

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:45.090
This world that we were
born in is our world.

00:13:45.090 --> 00:13:49.820
If you're the one who made this world,
then I have only thanks for you.

00:13:50.350 --> 00:13:52.930
Yeah, that's true. Sorry, sorry.

00:13:52.930 --> 00:13:55.980
Evelyn, we misunderstood a little.

00:13:57.310 --> 00:13:59.080
Why are you smiling?

00:13:59.610 --> 00:14:02.020
Once you've let out all the poison,
you feel better, don't you?

00:14:03.070 --> 00:14:06.630
The dream world is the best.
Because it's your own world.

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:09.320
But, it's poisonous.

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:17.410
For me, Haruto acknowledged
the poison that was my revenge,

00:14:17.410 --> 00:14:18.510
and I was saved.

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:22.760
Yes...

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:28.010
Haruto accepted everything about us.

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:33.100
He never walked ahead of us,
but always stayed by our side.

00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:37.740
That's why we are here next to you, Eve.

00:14:39.560 --> 00:14:42.060
Eve's heart is calming down.

00:14:42.060 --> 00:14:44.690
You can tell? Because you're Eve, too?

00:14:44.690 --> 00:14:45.420
Yes.

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:50.280
Evelyn, we keep talking about men,
but they're basically all scumbags.

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:52.950
And so immature. I totally get it.

00:14:52.950 --> 00:14:56.450
When I was young, it was
something of a status symbol

00:14:56.450 --> 00:14:59.960
to have different men driving you
around and paying for your meals.

00:14:59.960 --> 00:15:01.750
I've heard of that.

00:15:01.750 --> 00:15:04.000
I'd like to try it...!

00:15:05.460 --> 00:15:07.760
That's not the kind of
person you are, Yukorin.

00:15:09.930 --> 00:15:12.380
I can really relax around you all.

00:15:13.680 --> 00:15:17.770
Now that I think about it,
ever since I was thrown out of Eden,

00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:21.270
I just obeyed Adam and didn't have
a place where I could be myself.

00:15:22.350 --> 00:15:23.770
I wonder what this is...

00:15:23.770 --> 00:15:26.690
It's fine, isn't it?
Eve's calmed down, anyway.

00:15:26.690 --> 00:15:28.780
Would you like some of this?

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:30.170
It's delicious.

00:15:31.490 --> 00:15:33.250
She'll be able to tell once she tries some!

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:47.250
How is it? It's delicious, isn't it?

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:50.970
Yes. It's delicious.

00:15:50.970 --> 00:15:53.970
Delicious things make people happy.

00:15:53.970 --> 00:15:58.110
You probably couldn't even taste it
before because you were so angry.

00:16:00.930 --> 00:16:03.650
She said it's because you
changed your perspective.

00:16:04.610 --> 00:16:05.730
I see...

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:08.610
Let's keep that power in reserve.

00:16:08.860 --> 00:16:12.610
There may be many more things
that you won't be able to bear.

00:16:12.820 --> 00:16:15.370
During those times, you can
break things with all your might.

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:16.950
I will help, too.

00:16:17.450 --> 00:16:20.290
Everyone has times where they
just have to scream, right?

00:16:20.290 --> 00:16:23.960
It's a waste to go crazy
right after waking up.

00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:27.750
So learn about this world first,
and then go crazy...

00:16:27.750 --> 00:16:29.000
Is that what you mean?

00:16:30.170 --> 00:16:35.990
Very well. I will learn about
this world where you live.

00:16:36.600 --> 00:16:37.420
It's decided, then!

00:16:37.930 --> 00:16:39.260
Want to go eat something?

00:16:39.260 --> 00:16:41.230
Let's go to an all-you-can-eat place!

00:16:41.230 --> 00:16:42.560
It's gotta be karaoke!

00:16:42.560 --> 00:16:44.310
I'll do a medley of my songs!

00:16:44.310 --> 00:16:47.690
It's been a while,
but I feel like skating again.

00:16:47.690 --> 00:16:50.990
If I'm here, my legs will still let me jump.

00:16:51.610 --> 00:16:54.070
Why don't we get you a bank account?

00:16:54.070 --> 00:16:56.820
It's fun to just take leisurely walks, too.

00:16:57.530 --> 00:16:59.490
Why don't you try everything?

00:17:00.620 --> 00:17:01.630
I will.

00:17:12.550 --> 00:17:14.040
Do you feel better?

00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:16.430
It's still too soon.

00:17:16.430 --> 00:17:19.640
But don't you feel like
everything's become kind of silly?

00:17:21.390 --> 00:17:23.390
I suppose so...

00:17:32.860 --> 00:17:33.930
They're gone...

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:37.290
Does that mean those girls won?

00:17:39.410 --> 00:17:40.240
Eve...

00:17:41.620 --> 00:17:42.340
Lily...

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:46.460
You and I are one.

00:17:46.870 --> 00:17:47.580
I know.

00:17:48.210 --> 00:17:53.010
Even in a world like this, humans grow up.

00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:56.770
There are many things
they worry about, or fail at.

00:17:57.680 --> 00:17:59.760
They have also brought about many tragedies.

00:18:00.390 --> 00:18:03.300
However, humans are moving forward.

00:18:03.930 --> 00:18:04.590
Yes.

00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:10.470
I want you to teach me how we can
watch over this world together.

00:18:11.820 --> 00:18:16.280
I want you to teach me about
the world and the people you saw

00:18:16.740 --> 00:18:19.320
when I was bound by hatred.

00:18:20.410 --> 00:18:24.010
Right now, I am wavering
because of the witches' words.

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:30.330
That's fine. Humans passed
the time wavering like that.

00:18:31.590 --> 00:18:34.290
Adam and Eve were the first humans.

00:18:35.050 --> 00:18:38.760
So wavering is a manifestation
of that humanity?

00:18:39.130 --> 00:18:40.570
As is the you right now.

00:18:49.440 --> 00:18:51.060
Beyond that door,

00:18:51.690 --> 00:18:54.290
is a world that humans cannot imagine.

00:18:55.230 --> 00:18:57.950
Transcending time and space,

00:18:57.950 --> 00:18:59.450
God's domain.

00:19:02.370 --> 00:19:04.700
Brother, kill Eve.

00:19:04.990 --> 00:19:06.750
After all this?!

00:19:06.750 --> 00:19:08.620
Who'd be able to say it like that?

00:19:08.620 --> 00:19:10.040
There's no way I can kill Eve.

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:11.460
You just have to do that thing!

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:12.840
The thing you did to me.

00:19:13.170 --> 00:19:13.960
It can't be!

00:19:13.960 --> 00:19:15.840
She just did it with Lily, didn't she?

00:19:15.840 --> 00:19:19.130
She did that to herself,
so I think it's different.

00:19:19.510 --> 00:19:21.340
Sully Eve's purity.

00:19:21.340 --> 00:19:24.220
If you do that, then Eve
will become a normal girl.

00:19:24.560 --> 00:19:26.470
Not a goddess, but a human.

00:19:29.390 --> 00:19:30.480
Wait a minute.

00:19:30.770 --> 00:19:31.770
What's wrong?

00:19:31.770 --> 00:19:34.770
I know. It's hard 'cause
everyone's watching, right?

00:19:34.770 --> 00:19:35.980
That's not it.

00:19:36.570 --> 00:19:38.360
Lily's wish will come true.

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:42.490
Eve's anger also seems to have
calmed down thanks to you all.

00:19:42.490 --> 00:19:43.920
Yes. And?

00:19:44.450 --> 00:19:45.480
What about me?

00:19:45.990 --> 00:19:48.000
How can I wake up?

00:19:49.540 --> 00:19:52.000
Can I go past that door, too?

00:19:52.370 --> 00:19:54.130
What are you saying?

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:56.120
You finally found yourself!

00:19:56.960 --> 00:19:58.590
I want this dream to end.

00:19:58.590 --> 00:20:02.890
She said that beyond that door
is something humans can't imagine.

00:20:02.890 --> 00:20:04.430
What're you gonna do over there?

00:20:04.930 --> 00:20:06.290
I want to see it.

00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:09.020
I've been dreaming this whole time, anyway.

00:20:09.560 --> 00:20:12.060
If that's the case, I want to try
going to the world of a different dream.

00:20:12.230 --> 00:20:14.560
She didn't say it was a dream.

00:20:14.560 --> 00:20:15.630
It's fine.

00:20:16.400 --> 00:20:17.930
Thanks, everyone.

00:20:18.480 --> 00:20:20.360
As for Eve...

00:20:20.360 --> 00:20:22.070
Well, I'll do something about her.

00:20:22.610 --> 00:20:23.860
Something?

00:20:23.860 --> 00:20:25.660
I'll go with you.

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:27.830
Brother, you're coming, too?

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:29.930
It's something only I can do, right?

00:20:31.370 --> 00:20:32.210
Probably.

00:20:35.630 --> 00:20:38.460
You're going to go, just like that?

00:20:39.340 --> 00:20:41.810
I know where I am now.

00:20:42.300 --> 00:20:43.960
So I can come back anytime.

00:20:44.470 --> 00:20:45.630
That's what I'd like to think.

00:20:46.550 --> 00:20:49.400
Go visit me sometime.

00:20:50.020 --> 00:20:51.280
Very well.

00:20:52.180 --> 00:20:54.840
Be well... Although, I guess that's
a strange thing to say to you.

00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:58.610
Tell me about that world when you get back.

00:20:59.230 --> 00:20:59.860
Later.

00:21:14.370 --> 00:21:15.590
He left...

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:18.530
Have a nice trip.

00:21:30.010 --> 00:21:32.600
Man, I haven't heard anything.

00:21:32.890 --> 00:21:34.890
Did you go into the dream world?

00:21:34.890 --> 00:21:38.900
I did, but I couldn't go
to Haruto's room anymore.

00:21:38.900 --> 00:21:40.920
I can't find him anywhere, either.

00:21:41.690 --> 00:21:43.530
You know what I think?

00:21:43.530 --> 00:21:44.610
What?

00:21:45.240 --> 00:21:49.620
Since there was an Eve,
there should be an Adam, too, right?

00:21:49.620 --> 00:21:52.200
What if Haruto's Adam?

00:21:52.200 --> 00:21:55.460
No way, no way. Haruto is Haruto.

00:21:55.750 --> 00:21:59.790
Maybe only that girl, Lily,
knows the answer.

00:22:05.050 --> 00:22:07.480
We meet again, Brother.
